I left out the `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Importing HTTP would exceed that grant, and sending the input text to an external host would move data out of the node. Once the graph definition grants the capability, the fetch can be added. The output contract is unaffected.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

